1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,100
Vouch is a deli site whose assistant may never tell you food is safe to eat.

2
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:13,800
Nothing is ticked, so nothing is checked. No dish carries a verdict nobody asked for.

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:19,300
Thirty-four dishes, every ingredient published. All of this works with JavaScript off.

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:26,000
Tick dairy-free. Thirty-four dishes: fifteen unsafe, three we can't tell, sixteen with no conflict found.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,500
The Reuben: unsafe, through Swiss cheese. The Pastrami: no conflict found. Nothing here is ever called safe.

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:42,700
The Turkey club: dairy, through brioche bun, brioche, butter. Three steps down, inside a bun, invisible in the line you'd read.

7
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:48,200
Now let a model answer. The model proposes; a deterministic gate decides.

8
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:58,600
A replayed reply giving a false all-clear. Three claims withheld: one the checker contradicted, two it couldn't derive. The gate suppresses true statements too.

9
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:05,300
A deliberately broken network, refused. The validator's words are quoted exactly, kept apart from ours.

10
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:13,700
Running another site's agents asks first, names the origin, and says plainly: this runs their code in your browser.

11
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:20,400
Approved. The bakery's network loads from its own origin. Nothing it says changes a verdict.

12
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:28,300
Sixteen events, written down: every router choice, every action, every receipt. The refusal and the consent among them.

13
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:37,900
The conformance CLI checks any agentic site against the spec. Fourteen of fourteen here, and it names the six it didn't make.

14
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,500
Model proposes. Gate decides. Evidence survives. Apache-2.0, and live now.
